# ord of j-1728 at the place j=1728 is 1

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.ord_jLinePlace1728_jGen_sub`
(`072344ea-db1b-58f9-8f2e-461269728261`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `63891d12-67e2-592c-b503-7d0520ead616`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Work in the simple extension $\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the
transcendental element [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), a field which is
therefore a rational function field in one variable over $\mathbb{Q}$;
[`ModularCurve.jGen`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L268) denotes the generator $j_q$ regarded as an
element of this field. The place
[`ModularCurve.jLinePlace1728`](def/ModularCurve_JLinePlaces.html#L50) is the place of
$\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ — that is, a valuation subring containing
$\mathbb{Q}$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring — obtained by transporting,
along the ring isomorphism [`ModularCurve.jLineRingEquiv : RatFunc ℚ ≃+*
ℚ⟮jq⟯`](def/ModularCurve_JLinePlaces.html#L36) which carries the variable to $j_q$ and fixes
$\mathbb{Q}$, the finite place of $\mathbb{Q}(T)$ attached to the irreducible polynomial $T - 1728$.
For a place $v$ and an element $f$, $v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ is minus the logarithm of the value of $f$
under the adic valuation of the height-one prime of the valuation subring of $v$. The assertion is
that the order of $j_q - 1728$ at this place equals $1$: the function $j - 1728$ has a simple zero
at the point $j = 1728$ of the $j$-line.

This records one of the standard local normalisations on the $j$-line: $j-1728$ is a uniformiser at
the point $j=1728$, the point below which the covering $X_0(N)\to X(1)$ has its ramification of
order dividing $2$. It is used in
[`ModularCurve.ramificationIndex_eq_ord_sub_of_restrict_eq_jLinePlace1728`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.ramificationIndex_eq_ord_sub_of_restrict_eq_jLinePlace1728),
where ramification indices above $j=1728$ are computed as orders of $j-1728$ at places of the larger
function field.

